IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `col-limitation`

-- Choice of Law (Limitation Periods) Act 1993 (NSW) -- worked cases for every exported question in col-limitation.l4.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each
-- assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are illustrative: the
-- commencement date (1 March 1994) and the New Zealand declaration (taking effect 1 July 1995) used here are NOT the real
-- proclamation dates, which are not deposited.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`

-- Illustrative dates.
`commencement` MEANS `d` 1 3 1994
`NZ declaration` MEANS `d` 1 7 1995

`State` MEANS `another Australian State`
`Territory` MEANS `an Australian Territory`
`NZ` MEANS `New Zealand`
`NSW` MEANS `New South Wales`
`overseas` MEANS `a country other than New Zealand`

`NSW court` MEANS `a court of New South Wales`
`NSW arbitration` MEANS `an arbitrator, in an arbitration held in New South Wales`
`arbitration elsewhere` MEANS `an arbitrator, in an arbitration held outside New South Wales`
`court elsewhere` MEANS `a court outside New South Wales`

`in time` MEANS `section 5 applies, and I started in time under that place's limitation law`
`out of time` MEANS `section 5 applies, and the time that place's limitation law allows has passed`
`no s 5` MEANS `section 5 does not apply to my claim`
`not settled` MEANS `this Act does not settle it`

§§ `s 3 -- limitation law`

-- Arguments: limits, excludes or bars; by reference to when proceedings or arbitration are commenced.
#ASSERT `Is it a limitation law` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it a limitation law` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is it a limitation law` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is it a limitation law` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 4, 7 -- application`

-- Arguments: place, day instituted, day the Act commenced, declared for New Zealand, day the declaration took effect.
-- s 4: instituted on the commencement day is not "before" it (fork F1); the day before is.
#ASSERT `Does this Act apply to my proceedings` `State` (`d` 1 3 1994) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this Act apply to my proceedings` `State` (`d` 28 2 1994) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does this Act apply to my proceedings` `Territory` (`d` 2 3 1994) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Claims governed by NSW or overseas law: ss 4 and 7 do not exclude the proceedings (ss 5, 6 then give nothing).
#ASSERT `Does this Act apply to my proceedings` `NSW` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this Act apply to my proceedings` `overseas` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 7(1): no declaration for New Zealand, so the Act does not apply in relation to it.
#ASSERT `Does this Act apply to my proceedings` `NZ` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 7(2): instituted on the day the declaration takes effect applies; the day before does not.
#ASSERT `Does this Act apply to my proceedings` `NZ` (`d` 1 7 1995) `commencement` TRUE `NZ declaration` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this Act apply to my proceedings` `NZ` (`d` 30 6 1995) `commencement` TRUE `NZ declaration` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A declaration made by the commencing proclamation (s 7(1), second sentence); proceedings before it: both s 4 and s 7(2).
#ASSERT `Does this Act apply to my proceedings` `NZ` (`d` 28 2 1994) `commencement` TRUE `commencement` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does this Act apply to my proceedings` `NZ` (`d` 1 3 1994) `commencement` TRUE `commencement` EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 5 -- the other place's limitation law applied`

-- Arguments: place, forum, day instituted, day commenced, declared for NZ, declaration day, limits or bars, by reference
-- to commencement of proceedings.
#ASSERT `Will the court apply the other place's limitation law` `State` `NSW court` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Will the court apply the other place's limitation law` `Territory` `NSW arbitration` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Will the court apply the other place's limitation law` `NZ` `NSW court` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commencement` TRUE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Will the court apply the other place's limitation law` `NZ` `NSW court` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Will the court apply the other place's limitation law` `NZ` `NSW court` (`d` 30 6 1995) `commencement` TRUE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Will the court apply the other place's limitation law` `NSW` `NSW court` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Will the court apply the other place's limitation law` `overseas` `NSW court` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Will the court apply the other place's limitation law` `State` `court elsewhere` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An arbitrator outside NSW: is it "a court of the State"? Open (fork F2).
#ASSERT `Will the court apply the other place's limitation law` `State` `arbitration elsewhere` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A failed condition beats the open one.
#ASSERT `Will the court apply the other place's limitation law` `NSW` `arbitration elsewhere` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Will the court apply the other place's limitation law` `State` `arbitration elsewhere` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 4: proceedings instituted the day before commencement.
#ASSERT `Will the court apply the other place's limitation law` `State` `NSW court` (`d` 28 2 1994) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 3: a law that does not work by reference to the commencement of proceedings is no limitation law.
#ASSERT `Will the court apply the other place's limitation law` `State` `NSW court` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Will the court apply the other place's limitation law` `State` `NSW court` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 5 with the other place's period -- does it stop my claim`

-- Arguments: as for s 5, then the day the cause of action arose and the last day that law allows.
-- Cause of action 1 January 2020, last day 1 January 2026 (illustrative): instituted on the last day is in time; the
-- day after is not; the day before is.
#ASSERT `Does the other place's time limit stop my claim` `State` `NSW court` (`d` 1 1 2026) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 1 2020) (`d` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Does the other place's time limit stop my claim` `State` `NSW court` (`d` 2 1 2026) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 1 2020) (`d` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `out of time`
#ASSERT `Does the other place's time limit stop my claim` `State` `NSW court` (`d` 31 12 2025) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 1 2020) (`d` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `in time`
-- s 4: a cause of action that arose before commencement (1 January 1993) is within the Act; proceedings 1 January 1998
-- against a last day of 1 January 1999 are in time.
#ASSERT `Does the other place's time limit stop my claim` `Territory` `NSW court` (`d` 1 1 1998) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 1 1993) (`d` 1 1 1999) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Does the other place's time limit stop my claim` `Territory` `NSW court` (`d` 1 6 1994) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 1 1990) (`d` 1 1 1993) EQUALS `out of time`
-- Across a leap day: arose 29 February 2020, last day 28 February 2023; 1 March 2023 is too late.
#ASSERT `Does the other place's time limit stop my claim` `State` `NSW arbitration` (`d` 1 3 2023) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE (`d` 29 2 2020) (`d` 28 2 2023) EQUALS `out of time`
#ASSERT `Does the other place's time limit stop my claim` `State` `NSW arbitration` (`d` 28 2 2023) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE (`d` 29 2 2020) (`d` 28 2 2023) EQUALS `in time`
-- New Zealand after the declaration.
#ASSERT `Does the other place's time limit stop my claim` `NZ` `NSW court` (`d` 1 7 2021) `commencement` TRUE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 7 2015) (`d` 1 7 2021) EQUALS `in time`
-- s 5 not applying.
#ASSERT `Does the other place's time limit stop my claim` `NSW` `NSW court` (`d` 2 1 2026) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 1 2020) (`d` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `no s 5`
#ASSERT `Does the other place's time limit stop my claim` `overseas` `NSW court` (`d` 2 1 2026) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 1 2020) (`d` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `no s 5`
#ASSERT `Does the other place's time limit stop my claim` `NZ` `NSW court` (`d` 2 1 2026) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 1 2020) (`d` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `no s 5`
#ASSERT `Does the other place's time limit stop my claim` `State` `NSW court` (`d` 28 2 1994) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 1 1990) (`d` 1 1 1993) EQUALS `no s 5`
#ASSERT `Does the other place's time limit stop my claim` `State` `court elsewhere` (`d` 2 1 2026) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 1 2020) (`d` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `no s 5`
#ASSERT `Does the other place's time limit stop my claim` `State` `NSW court` (`d` 2 1 2026) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2020) (`d` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `no s 5`
-- An arbitrator outside NSW (fork F2).
#ASSERT `Does the other place's time limit stop my claim` `State` `arbitration elsewhere` (`d` 2 1 2026) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 1 2020) (`d` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `not settled`

§§ `s 6 -- a discretion under that law`

-- Arguments: place whose limitation law it is, forum, day instituted, day commenced, declared for NZ, declaration day,
-- limits or bars, by reference to commencement, the court is exercising a discretion that law confers.
#ASSERT `Must the court use the discretion as that place's courts do` `State` `NSW court` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the court use the discretion as that place's courts do` `State` `NSW court` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the court use the discretion as that place's courts do` `Territory` `NSW arbitration` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the court use the discretion as that place's courts do` `NZ` `NSW court` (`d` 1 7 1995) `commencement` TRUE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the court use the discretion as that place's courts do` `NZ` `NSW court` (`d` 30 6 1995) `commencement` TRUE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the court use the discretion as that place's courts do` `overseas` `NSW court` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the court use the discretion as that place's courts do` `NSW` `NSW court` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the court use the discretion as that place's courts do` `State` `court elsewhere` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the court use the discretion as that place's courts do` `State` `arbitration elsewhere` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Must the court use the discretion as that place's courts do` `State` `arbitration elsewhere` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the court use the discretion as that place's courts do` `State` `NSW court` (`d` 28 2 1994) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the court use the discretion as that place's courts do` `State` `NSW court` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commencement` FALSE `NZ declaration` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
